$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Part B: Compound 1913A (380 mg, 1.55 mmol) and
hydrazine (0.15 ml, 4.6 mmol) were dissolved in EtOH (30 ml). The
reaction mixture was stirred at 100°C for 19 h. The mixture was cooled to
25°C and the precipitates were filtered and washed with cold EtOH.
Compound 1919A was prepared from methyl 4-iodobenzoate by using a
procedure described in Part B of Example 130.
